[thin] These 1.540 mm nearest-surface readings run diagonally from the narrowed rear body's upper outer corner to the front roof surround's inner end corner. In machine coordinates the east pair is (91.25, 199.786, 348.652) to (89.75, 199.75, 349.0); frame coordinates subtract Y164.55 and Z299.9. Native horizontal sections through the rear pick retain X82.8..91.25, or 8.45 mm of stock, through Z346..348.978. Immediately above Z349 that rear region is empty; ahead of Y199.75 the upper surround retains X89.75..98.25, or 8.50 mm. The short diagonal is real material at the meeting of those two broad sections; it does not identify a finite 1.5 mm rear wall. The complete 3 mm brim-bearing plane remains beneath the silicone. The source-bound native corner sections are recorded in ../../enclosure/enclosure/y-seam-plain-review.json.
alternatives: Widening the rear body enters back-top's corner-block passage, which retains 0.25 mm running clearance. Removing the bearing below Z349 would reduce the agreed full silicone-brim support. A cut confined to the rear above Z349 removes no material there. The two broad sections retain their square functional ends rather than adding a local blend around the diagnostic's diagonal.
