[thin] These 1.518 mm readings follow a diagonal across the junction between the central frame body and each blunt front foot wing. The first pick at X±98.016 lies inside the retained body boundary X±98.25 on the corbel underside; the other is the wing's upper root corner at local Y-47.759, Z7. The free wing ends on that plane with a full nominal 3 mm vertical section, Z4..7. The rail bearings stand at Z16.2, above this foot-wing junction. The diagnostic's short diagonal crosses the corner between the broad body and the nominal 3 mm end. The finite wing-end intervals and source-bound body and bearing regions are recorded in ../../enclosure/enclosure/y-seam-plain-review.json.
alternatives: Extending the cut inboard would remove the main body and under-flare stock. Moving the end forward would reduce its section below the nominal 3 mm; moving it farther aft would remove more of the wing. The straight 3 mm end keeps the broad body and the rail geometry.
